  "strategy": "Appraoch and rationale:\nThe core issue with the previous program is its reliance on heuristic local searches and optimization phases that lack global exploration. We introduce a multi-resolution strategy to avoid local optima and leverage mathematical guarantees through disciplined convex programming (DCP). The key new element is a global optimizer using CVXPY that explicitly bounds the maximum correlation via exponential penalty functions.\n\nMathematical specification:\nWe represent the function \\( h \\) with \\( n \\) points over a domain of length 2. The optimization domain is defined by \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\) and \\( \\sum_{i=1}^n h_i = n/2 \\). The objective to minimize is \\( C_5 = \\max_k \\left| \\int h(x)(1-h(x+k)) \\, dx \\right| \\).\n\nFor clarity, let \\( dx = 2/n \\) and discretize the integral:\n\\[\nC_n = \\max_k \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} h_i(1-h_{(i+k)_n})\n\\]\nwhere \\((i+k)_n\\) denotes modulo n periodic indexing.\n\nThe novel mathematical formulation penalizes large correlation values exponentially:\n\\[\n\\min_{h} \\left\\| \\{c_k - \\alpha\\} \\exp( -\\beta(c_k - \\alpha) ) \\right\\|_1\n\\]\nfor the \\(2n-1\\) fixed-range shifts \\(k\\). This ensures priority for reducing the dominant correlations while meeting the user-defined tolerance \\( \\alpha \\).\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Start from provided parent if available (`initial_h_values` is given)\n2. Formulate CVXPY program to minimize the penalized correlations subject to:\n   - Box constraints: \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\) for all i\n   - Linear constraint: \\( \\sum_i h_i = n/2 \\)\n   - Bounds on correlations: penalty parameters \\( \\alpha, \\beta \\)\n3. Use exponential cone transformations for penalty terms (via DCP)\n4. Solve using ECOS (within CVXPY) for small n=140\n5. If time allows, scale to n=280 via interpolation with reprojection\n6. Otherwise, use best solution under deadline\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- By default, use alpha=0.38 and beta=100 for penalty robustness\n- Optional variable: if parent provided, use it; else start uniform/eps-norm+L-BFGS\n- Scalers: 0.1 to 5.0 for alpha and beta if no parent provided\n- Random distributions involve uniform scaling and ADAM optimization for coarse search\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n- Phase0: 10s setup\n- Phase1: 50s CVXPY solve with parent\n- Phase2: 60s upscale if time remaining (using original unscaled solution)\n- Phase3 Trail: 400s fine-tuning (with exponential scheduling)\n- Robustness: preserve bounds by repair, track best solution under timeout\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- Check solution satisfies: 0<=h[i]<=1, sum(h)==70\n- Recheck C5 by calling compare in original task's evaluate\n- Output tuple: (h_values, c5_float, n_points)\n\nNow a detailed full implementation:",
